{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1357856-brainstorming-gift-of-oaths","id":1357856,"title":"Brainstorming: Gift of Oaths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-30T12:31:29-08:00","id":1357856,"title":"Brainstorming: Gift of Oaths","content":"While on a walk this morning, I attempted to think up a special ability for Changeling that would allow someone to break a Pledge without facing any consequences. Then, my brain suddenly decided to go another route, and I found myself coming up with a Werewolf Gift centered around oaths, promises, and laws.<br /> <br /> I wanted to share what I have so far and solicit some ideas for the various Facets. The general idea is to examine what promises look like from the point of view of Shadow symbolism, how they might play into the Sacred Hunt, Bans as a type of promise encoded into one's very Essence\u2014the expected suspects for this type of thing.<br /> <br /> Anyway:<br /> <br /> <b>Cunning: Crossed Fingers</b><br /> <br /> The werewolf can break a promise without consequence.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> Manipulation + Subterfuge + Cunning vs Composure + Primal Urge<br /> <br /> <b>Dramatic Failure: </b>The werewolf gains the Ban Condition of \u201cCannot take any action that would jeopardize the promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b>Failure:</b> The werewolf faces the normal consequences if he breaks the promise.<br /> <br /> <b>Success:</b> The werewolf can take one action that would break a promise or law without consequence. For mundane oaths, he faces no retribution (he might speed past a traffic cop and not get pulled over, for instance), while supernatural-backed promises ignore the violation, but only this once. This Facet does not prevent Breaking Points from violating the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> <b>Exceptional Success:</b> ???<br /> <br /> This is the first Facet I came up with. I think it fits pretty well, but probably needs some checking against various conditions. It's also currently a lot more useful in crossover settings where characters might have more ready access to various kinds of promise magic, but the mundane utility should still make it desirable even without Pledges, Carthian Laws, etc. I also currently am unsure of a suitable Exceptional Success effect. This Facet might also need a note about Clashes of Wills.<br /> <br /> <b>Glory: ???</b><br /> <br /> I have a few half-developed ideas for this Facet, but nothing fully concrete yet. I like the idea of this Facet &quot;marking&quot; the prey so that everyone instinctively knows that they've broken an oath (or, conversely, that they have upheld a particularly arduous promise). Alternately, it could be interesting to have a power that gives the user the Ban Condition in exchange for some boon, along the lines of flaring Renown. Or, since Glory likes big and dramatic effects, maybe this could be a high-Essence power that imposes some law over an entire territory that everyone instinctively knows, and/or to which the werewolf instinctively knows whenever is violated (that might be better suited for a Pack Rite, though).<br /> <br /> <b>Honor: ???</b><br /> <br /> Whatever this ends up being, I feel it needs to be special. Elodoth already have access to an oath-swearing power, and, although this Facet shouldn't build directly off it (as it risks excluding werewolves of other Auspices or Half-Moons who start with an alternate Moon Gift), it should keep that in mind. Some ideas I've had involve transferring a promise or Ban from one party to another, changing the terms of an oath or Ban, and learning about any oaths the prey has made or broken.<br /> <br /> <b>Purity: Punish the Oathbreaker</b><br /> <br /> The werewolf empowers himself to lay low those who would presume to violate sworn promises.<br /> <br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Essence<br /> <br /> <b>Action:</b> Reflexive<br /> <br /> <b>Dice Pool:</b> None<br /> <br /> To use this Facet, the werewolf must truly know that the prey has broken a sworn promise. This does not need to be a promise made to the werewolf himself; indeed, quite a few Rahu with this Facet find themselves in the role of hunting hounds, either sworn to a powerful and vengeful lord, or as chasseurs-for-hire. Blood Talons especially acquire this Facet to hunt down rogue Uratha who have violated the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> When activated, the werewolf adds his Purity to the next roll using a Power Attribute made against the prey.<br /> <br /> I like how this one turned out in general. Like many Purity facets, its effect is straightforward, and I feel that affecting Power Attributes in general allows for potentially interesting non-combat uses.<br /> <br /> <b>Wisdom: ???</b><br /> <br /> Whatever this ends of being, I feel it should interact with Bans in some way. My first idea was a Facet that alleviates the Ban Condition (but not naturally occurring Bans); my second was a power that alters the terms of the Ban, or shifting a Ban from one target to another. An always-on effect that automatically alerts the werewolf to when an action they're about to take would violate a promise they've made could also be interesting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:41:22-08:00","id":1357858,"title":"","content":"quick thought before I get back to work and come back later: this could be a Gift passed around as a temptation by Wound Spirits and Bale Hounds","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:47:21-08:00","id":1357861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1357856-brainstorming-gift-of-oaths?p=1357858#post1357858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">quick thought before I get back to work and come back later: this could be a Gift passed around as a temptation by Wound Spirits and Bale Hounds</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's a good point. I'll have to mull that over some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-30T12:53:35-08:00","id":1357864,"title":"","content":"yeah. I remember hearing that Totems don't tend to like Werewolves that circumvent their bans the normal way. this could either anger them more, or it could be like the Moon-shunned and they are literally unable to realize you broke the ban if you did it this way. Either way, Bans are a pivotal element of Shadow ecology/society. Something that could subvert them like this (and remember that Spirits can have gift-like abilities as Numina) could upend centuries-old power structures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-06T19:12:44-08:00","id":1359389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1357856-brainstorming-gift-of-oaths?p=1357864#post1357864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah. I remember hearing that Totems don't tend to like Werewolves that circumvent their bans the normal way. this could either anger them more, or it could be like the Moon-shunned and they are literally unable to realize you broke the ban if you did it this way. Either way, Bans are a pivotal element of Shadow ecology/society. Something that could subvert them like this (and remember that Spirits can have gift-like abilities as Numina) could upend centuries-old power structures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I'm a little cautious about this Gift being able to overturn natural Bans; if it does, it should be in a somewhat tricky way or with a twist of some sort. My intuition is that that sort of thing should be more the domain of Rites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}